        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die Bildschirmsynchronisierung im Kontrollzentrum nutzen, um dieses Visual auf einem Bildschirm zu zeigen"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Colour defaults to the heard tone octave-transposed into visible light — its frequency doubled until it reaches the visible band, rendered through CIE 1931 and closed over the CIE purple line where deep red meets deep violet, so every tone has a colour. Hue/Saturation rotate the palette for VJ/performance use. Motion is capped so the flash rate always stays under the 3 Hz safety limit." : {
      "comment" : "Panel text (E4-7, 2026-09-30): SwiftUI literal keys of EchoelStudioView, the instrument — localised by content, no Sources change.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Colour defaults to the heard tone octave-transposed into visible light — its frequency doubled until it reaches the visible band, rendered through CIE 1931 and closed over the CIE purple line where deep red meets deep violet, so every tone has a colour. Hue/Saturation rotate the palette for VJ/performance use. Motion is capped so the flash rate always stays under the 3 Hz safety limit."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die Farbe folgt standardmäßig dem gehörten Ton, oktavweise ins sichtbare Licht versetzt — seine Frequenz wird verdoppelt, bis sie das sichtbare Band erreicht, über CIE 1931 gerendert und über der CIE-Purpurlinie geschlossen, wo Tiefrot auf Tiefviolett trifft, sodass jeder Ton eine Farbe hat. Farbton/Sättigung drehen die Palette für VJ- und Performance-Zwecke. Die Bewegung ist begrenzt, damit die Blitzrate immer unter der 3-Hz-Sicherheitsgrenze bleibt."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "What your fingers sound like on the field. Same as music follows the generated music; pick a patch to give the field its own voice." : {
      "comment" : "Panel text (E4-7, 2026-09-30): SwiftUI literal keys of EchoelStudioView, the instrument — localised by content, no Sources change.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "What your fingers sound like on the field. Same as music follows the generated music; pick a patch to give the field its own voice."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Wie deine Finger auf dem Feld klingen. „Wie die Musik“ folgt der generierten Musik; wähle ein Patch, um dem Feld eine eigene Stimme zu geben."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Sliding the finger opens vibrato and ensemble width; Glide makes slides sing between notes instead of re-striking." : {
      "comment" : "Panel text (E4-7, 2026-09-30): SwiftUI literal keys of EchoelStudioView, the instrument — localised by content, no Sources change.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Sliding the finger opens vibrato and ensemble width; Glide makes slides sing between notes instead of re-striking."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Den Finger zu ziehen öffnet Vibrato und Ensemblebreite; Glide lässt Züge zwischen Noten singen, statt neu anzuschlagen."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The field plays itself while the transport runs: a point travels the surface — or, on Arp, walks your chord — and strikes notes in your key. Press Play to hear it. Put a finger down and it stops instantly — your hand always wins. Its speed follows the Sync grid above, even with Sync itself off." : {
      "comment" : "Panel text (E4-7, 2026-09-30): SwiftUI literal keys of EchoelStudioView, the instrument — localised by content, no Sources change.",
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The field plays itself while the transport runs: a point travels the surface — or, on Arp, walks your chord — and strikes notes in your key. Press Play to hear it. Put a finger down and it stops instantly — your hand always wins. Its speed follows the Sync grid above, even with Sync itself off."
          }
        },
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Das Feld spielt sich selbst, während der Transport läuft: ein Punkt wandert über die Fläche — oder läuft auf Arp deinen Akkord entlang — und schlägt Noten in deiner Tonart an. Abspielen drücken, um es zu hören. Ein Finger auf dem Feld stoppt es sofort — deine Hand gewinnt immer. Sein Tempo folgt dem Sync-Raster oben, auch wenn Sync selbst aus ist."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Motion" : {
      "comment" : "Panel text (E4-7, 2026-09-30): SwiftUI literal keys of EchoelStudioView, the instrument — localised by content, no Sources change.",
