    },
    "How fast your heart is beating right now." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Wie schnell dein Herz gerade schlägt."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "How fast your heart is beating right now."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The natural beat-to-beat variation in your heartbeat." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die natürliche Schwankung deines Herzschlags von Schlag zu Schlag."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The natural beat-to-beat variation in your heartbeat."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "A short-term HRV measure of moment-to-moment change." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Ein Kurzzeit-HRV-Maß für die Veränderung von Moment zu Moment."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "A short-term HRV measure of moment-to-moment change."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Overall HRV across the whole reading." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Gesamte HRV über die ganze Messung."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Overall HRV across the whole reading."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "How often consecutive beats differ by more than 50 ms." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Wie oft aufeinanderfolgende Schläge sich um mehr als 50 ms unterscheiden."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "How often consecutive beats differ by more than 50 ms."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "How much of your heartbeat gathers into one slow rhythm." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Wie sehr sich dein Herzschlag zu einem langsamen Rhythmus sammelt."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "How much of your heartbeat gathers into one slow rhythm."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Breaths per minute." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Atemzüge pro Minute."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Breaths per minute."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Beats per minute. It rises with effort, excitement or stress and falls with rest. In Echoelmusic your heart rate shapes the energy of the music — and, while the tempo follows your pulse, the tempo itself (a locked tempo stays where you set it)." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Schläge pro Minute. Sie steigt bei Anstrengung, Aufregung oder Stress und sinkt in Ruhe. In Echoelmusic formt deine Herzfrequenz die Energie der Musik — und, solange das Tempo deinem Puls folgt, das Tempo selbst (ein gesperrtes Tempo bleibt, wo du es gesetzt hast)."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Beats per minute. It rises with effort, excitement or stress and falls with rest. In Echoelmusic your heart rate shapes the energy of the music — and, while the tempo follows your pulse, the tempo itself (a locked tempo stays where you set it)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The tiny differences in time between one heartbeat and the next. Higher variability generally reflects a relaxed, adaptable state; lower variability often goes with stress or fatigue. Echoelmusic uses it to open or close the timbre. Reliable beat-to-beat HRV needs a chest strap; the camera shows it only when the reading is physiologically plausible, otherwise “—”." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Die winzigen Zeitunterschiede zwischen einem Herzschlag und dem nächsten. Höhere Variabilität spiegelt meist einen entspannten, anpassungsfähigen Zustand; niedrigere geht oft mit Stress oder Erschöpfung einher. Echoelmusic öffnet oder schließt damit die Klangfarbe. Verlässliche Schlag-zu-Schlag-HRV braucht einen Brustgurt; die Kamera zeigt sie nur, wenn die Messung physiologisch plausibel ist, sonst „—“."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The tiny differences in time between one heartbeat and the next. Higher variability generally reflects a relaxed, adaptable state; lower variability often goes with stress or fatigue. Echoelmusic uses it to open or close the timbre. Reliable beat-to-beat HRV needs a chest strap; the camera shows it only when the reading is physiologically plausible, otherwise “—”."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Root mean square of successive differences between heartbeats — a standard short-term HRV measure that mostly reflects your parasympathetic ‘rest-and-digest’ activity. Higher values often go with a more relaxed moment." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Quadratisches Mittel der aufeinanderfolgenden Differenzen zwischen Herzschlägen — ein Standard-Kurzzeit-HRV-Maß, das vor allem deine parasympathische ‚Ruhe-und-Verdauung‘-Aktivität widerspiegelt. Höhere Werte gehen oft mit einem entspannteren Moment einher."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Root mean square of successive differences between heartbeats — a standard short-term HRV measure that mostly reflects your parasympathetic ‘rest-and-digest’ activity. Higher values often go with a more relaxed moment."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Standard deviation of the time between normal heartbeats across the whole reading. It captures your total heart-rate variability from many sources at once." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Standardabweichung der Zeit zwischen normalen Herzschlägen über die ganze Messung. Sie erfasst deine gesamte Herzratenvariabilität aus vielen Quellen zugleich."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Standard deviation of the time between normal heartbeats across the whole reading. It captures your total heart-rate variability from many sources at once."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The percentage of consecutive heartbeats that differ by more than 50 milliseconds — another marker of parasympathetic activity. Higher values usually accompany a more relaxed moment." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Der Anteil aufeinanderfolgender Herzschläge, die sich um mehr als 50 Millisekunden unterscheiden — ein weiterer Marker parasympathischer Aktivität. Höhere Werte begleiten meist einen entspannteren Moment."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "The percentage of consecutive heartbeats that differ by more than 50 milliseconds — another marker of parasympathetic activity. Higher values usually accompany a more relaxed moment."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "How much of your heart-rate variability gathers into a single slow rhythm. Echoelmusic measures it as a real frequency spectrum of your heartbeat (most accurate with a chest strap), peaking around 0.1 Hz — roughly six breaths a minute. It tends to be highest during slow, steady breathing; higher coherence makes the music calmer and more spacious." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Wie sehr sich deine Herzratenvariabilität zu einem einzigen langsamen Rhythmus sammelt. Echoelmusic misst sie als echtes Frequenzspektrum deines Herzschlags (am genauesten mit Brustgurt), mit Spitze um 0,1 Hz — etwa sechs Atemzüge pro Minute. Sie ist meist bei langsamer, gleichmäßiger Atmung am höchsten; höhere Kohärenz macht die Musik ruhiger und weiter."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "How much of your heart-rate variability gathers into a single slow rhythm. Echoelmusic measures it as a real frequency spectrum of your heartbeat (most accurate with a chest strap), peaking around 0.1 Hz — roughly six breaths a minute. It tends to be highest during slow, steady breathing; higher coherence makes the music calmer and more spacious."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Your breathing rate. Slow breathing (about five to six breaths a minute) tends to raise coherence. Echoelmusic’s optional breathing guide paces it for you, and your breath phase shapes how the music moves." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Deine Atemfrequenz. Langsames Atmen (etwa fünf bis sechs Atemzüge pro Minute) hebt meist die Kohärenz. Der optionale Atem-Guide von Echoelmusic gibt dir den Takt vor, und deine Atemphase formt, wie sich die Musik bewegt."
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Your breathing rate. Slow breathing (about five to six breaths a minute) tends to raise coherence. Echoelmusic’s optional breathing guide paces it for you, and your breath phase shapes how the music moves."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "read your pulse to see it move" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Puls messen, um es sich bewegen zu sehen"
          }
        },
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "read your pulse to see it move"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "demo values, not your body" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "de" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
